    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_42bb092b6696f59c15a9f036c60add3d077a6ce88890188c6a1adaa2f69e1cd0",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Equation (9) supports an incidence decomposition of the correction on pk: under coprimality, marked divisors inherited from k form one channel and the newly introduced prime p forms another. This split lets N31 reuse the N2-type triple-integral reduction and N32 reuse the N1-type double-integral reduction with P_1(v), gaining modular analytic templates while retaining that neither channel alone is the full shifted-side correction. The extracted text does not safely identify which gcd class is placed in the error.",
